      "side": 1,
      "message": "Please fix this WARNING reported by autoreview issue finding: When wrapping a borrowed WGPUDevice handle from JNI into a wgpu::Device RAII object, you must increment the reference count. Without this, the local RAII object\u0027s destructor will eventually decrement the reference count that the Java object expects to own, leading to a potential use-after-free.\n\nAdd `outDevice-\u003eReference();` after the assignment.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 109,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 109,
        "endChar": 0
      },
      "revId": "cc7bd81810b44d8508b707ab3bd115cd3adea053",
