      "lineNbr": 440,
      "author": {
        "id": 4269882
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-06-16T19:12:47Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Assigning endState.fences[i] to a local wgpu::SharedFence variable is actually safe here. The C++ wrapper automatically increments the reference count when the variable is created, and decrements it when the variable goes out of scope. This means it cleans up after itself without causing a double-release.",
      "parentUuid": "012a7318_29a8cee0",
