      },
      "lineNbr": 458,
      "author": {
        "id": 4269882
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-06-16T19:12:47Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The FreeMembers() function is actually a private method in the C++ struct. The struct\u0027s destructor automatically calls FreeMembers() when it goes out of scope. If we call it manually, it wouldn\u0027t compile and would lead to a double-free, so the wrapper is safely handling this cleanup behind the scenes.",
      "parentUuid": "98e8e4e9_a5c226ac",
